{"ts":"2026-05-07T18:05:43.282376Z","stage_idx":4,"tool":"request_spec_revision","args":{"reason":"The faithfulness metric as specified (ablating the complement of the circuit) yields very low values even with expanded circuits. On dev split:\n- Top-3 heads: faithfulness = -0.79 (clipped to 0.0)\n- Top-7 heads: faithfulness = -0.13 (clipped to 0.0)  \n- Top-10 heads: faithfulness = 0.017\n- Top-20 heads (all with positive recovery): faithfulness = 0.11\n\nThe issue is that mean-ablating 124-141 heads destroys too much model capacity, causing circuit-only performance to drop below even the corrupted baseline. The joint patch recovery from top-3 heads is excellent (0.97), confirming the heads are causally important, but the faithfulness measure (circuit-only vs full model) doesn't reach the 0.85 threshold.\n\nThis suggests either: (1) the faithfulness formula/method needs revision (perhaps partial ablation or different baseline), (2) the circuit definition should include more supporting infrastructure, or (3) the 0.85 threshold is too strict for this ablation-based faithfulness measure on GPT-2-small's IOI task.\n\nRecommendation: Revise to use patch-recovery as the primary circuit validation metric (which we pass at 0.97) rather than complement-ablation faithfulness, or adjust the faithfulness computation method.","prior_results_ref":null},"ok":true,"result_summary":"revision requested; run terminal","budget_after":{"tool_calls":19,"bash_calls":0,"gpu_seconds":0.0,"wallclock_seconds":0.0,"samples":0}}
